---
<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap" data-core-duration="70–80 minutes" data-extension-duration="15–20 minutes">
  <a class="back" href="/curriculum/#lvl-B2">Back to curriculum</a>
  <p class="overline">B2 Vocabulary · Figurative meaning, grammar, and pragmatic fit</p>
  <h1>Idioms & fixed expressions</h1>
  <p class="lede">An idiom is useful only when it makes the listener's job easier. Learn the whole pattern, infer it from evidence, and know when plain language is the stronger choice.</p>
  <p class="note-line"><b>Can-do:</b> By the end, you can distinguish literal meaning, idiomatic meaning, collocation, conversational routine, and semi-fixed frame without forcing every chunk into one label; infer an unfamiliar expression from outcome, contrast, speaker attitude, and conversational purpose; use a selective bank of common expressions with their fixed articles, prepositions, complements, pronoun slots, and verb forms; recognize acceptable grammatical and regional variation; distinguish alignment, recognition, initiation, progress, effort, boundaries, skepticism, flexible planning, and temporary stopping; avoid idiom overload and dismissive clichés; shift from internal conversation to precise client, safety, academic, and formal-record language; hear U.S. rhythm, reductions, linking, and contrastive prominence; and tell a coherent project story in which every expression earns its place.</p>

  <h2>Retrieve the language this lesson depends on</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You recovered conventional partnership, concession, shared context, audience-sensitive register, and evidence-calibrated wording before interpreting figurative chunks.">
    <h3>Five prerequisite decisions</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Idiom prerequisite choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="conventional partnership">conventional partnership</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Nevertheless">Nevertheless</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="shared context">shared context</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a literal process description">a literal process description</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a bounded claim">a bounded claim</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="as many idioms as possible">as many idioms as possible</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>English uses <span class="ex">make a decision</span> because <span class="ex">make + decision</span> is a conventional <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="conventional partnership" data-hint="Choose the lexical relationship that makes one grammatical combination sound established." data-fix="Make a decision is a conventional partnership, or collocation.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The plan was difficult to carry out. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Nevertheless" data-hint="Use the marker that acknowledges difficulty and introduces a counterexpected result." data-fix="The plan was difficult to carry out. Nevertheless, the team completed it.">choose</button>, the team completed it.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>An efficient internal chat can use more conversational language because teammates have <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="shared context" data-hint="Choose the relationship condition that lets a short expression remain recoverable." data-fix="Shared context can support concise conversational language.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>A safety instruction should normally prefer <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a literal process description" data-hint="Choose wording that minimizes interpretive effort when consequences are serious." data-fix="Safety-critical instructions should state the process literally.">choose</button> over a culture-specific metaphor.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>When a small pilot shows limited improvement, <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a bounded claim" data-hint="Match the language strength to the evidence rather than using a dramatic expression." data-fix="A bounded claim preserves the pilot's scope and uncertainty.">choose</button> is more accurate than saying the project has completely changed the game.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice: the situation does most of the explaining</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Fictional Alder Street Museum launch chat</h3>
    <p><b>Maya, project lead:</b> Before we get the ball rolling, let's make sure we're on the same page. The staff preview is October 12, and the public launch is October 19.</p>
    <p><b>Eli, operations:</b> The new entrance ramp missed the required clearance by one inch. We can adjust the schedule, but I draw the line at cutting corners on accessibility.</p>
    <p><b>Maya:</b> The supplier went the extra mile and agreed to deliver a revised ramp by October 10 without an added labor charge.</p>
    <p><b>Nora, ticketing:</b> Today's test duplicated 7 of 120 orders in one payment connector. Are we back to square one?</p>
    <p><b>Maya:</b> No. The other systems still work. We need to rebuild one connector. After the next staging test, we can say “so far, so good” if the duplicate orders stop, but that will not guarantee live performance.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You inferred launch initiation, shared dates, an accessibility boundary, extra contractual effort, an exaggerated restart, and a provisional positive update from the surrounding events.">
    <h3>Discovery check: infer purpose before definition</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Alder Street discovery choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="start the coordinated work">start the coordinated work</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="share the same dates and expectations">share the same dates and expectations</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="refuse to sacrifice the accessibility standard">refuse to sacrifice the accessibility standard</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="provide more help than the contract required">provide more help than the contract required</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="restart the entire project from the beginning">restart the entire project from the beginning</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="report encouraging progress without promising final success">report encouraging progress without promising final success</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="translate every noun literally">translate every noun literally</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span><span class="ex">Get the ball rolling</span> means <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="start the coordinated work" data-hint="Use Maya's timing before the team begins the project discussion." data-fix="Maya uses get the ball rolling to start the coordinated work.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span><span class="ex">Be on the same page</span> means <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="share the same dates and expectations" data-hint="The next sentence makes two dates explicit so everyone understands the plan alike." data-fix="The team needs to share the same dates and expectations.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span><span class="ex">Draw the line at cutting corners</span> means <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="refuse to sacrifice the accessibility standard" data-hint="Eli allows a schedule change but rejects lowering one requirement." data-fix="Eli refuses to sacrifice the accessibility standard.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span><span class="ex">Went the extra mile</span> means <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="provide more help than the contract required" data-hint="The source identifies an earlier delivery and no extra labor charge beyond the supplier's obligation." data-fix="The supplier provided more help than the contract required.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span><span class="ex">Back to square one</span> would mean <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="restart the entire project from the beginning" data-hint="Maya rejects the phrase because only one connector needs rebuilding." data-fix="Back to square one means restarting from the beginning, which overstates this limited fault.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span><span class="ex">So far, so good</span> can <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="report encouraging progress without promising final success" data-hint="The phrase evaluates progress up to the present checkpoint, not future live operation." data-fix="So far, so good reports encouraging progress to date without guaranteeing the future.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Get to the root: infer the whole chunk from its job</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Not every conventional chunk is equally idiomatic. Labels overlap across dictionaries and teaching traditions. The useful question is: what does the whole expression do here, and which parts can change without losing that function?</p>
  <table><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Example</th><th>What to learn</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td>literal phrase</td><td>cut the paper's corners</td><td>ordinary word meanings identify a physical action</td></tr>
    <tr><td>figurative idiom</td><td>cut corners on safety</td><td>the conventional whole means sacrifice standards to save time, effort, or money</td></tr>
    <tr><td>collocation</td><td>reach a decision</td><td>the partnership is conventional even though the meaning is mostly transparent</td></tr>
    <tr><td>conversational routine</td><td>That rings a bell.</td><td>the complete response manages recognition in interaction</td></tr>
    <tr><td>semi-fixed frame</td><td>keep someone in the loop</td><td>the grammar stays recognizable while one participant slot changes</td></tr>
    <tr><td>proverb-like response</td><td>Easier said than done.</td><td>the compact evaluation can stand as a response to a proposal</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <div class="note"><h3>Use four clues before opening a dictionary</h3><ol><li><b>Literal fit:</b> Would the physical meaning make sense here?</li><li><b>Outcome:</b> What happened before and after the phrase?</li><li><b>Attitude:</b> Is the speaker aligning, warning, praising, criticizing, doubting, or closing?</li><li><b>Paraphrase:</b> Which plain sentence preserves the same claim and strength?</li></ol><p>Then confirm meaning, grammar, region, and register in a reliable dictionary or corpus. Context gives a hypothesis; reference evidence tests it.</p></div>
  <div class="note"><h3>Recognition can come before active use</h3><p>You may understand an expression without needing to produce it. Prioritize common chunks that solve a real conversational problem. Keep less familiar, highly regional, dated, offensive, or specialized expressions in your recognition vocabulary until repeated evidence shows where they belong.</p></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You inferred recognition, unstated meaning, central meaning, social initiation, project initiation, partial progress, basic procedures, implementation difficulty, delayed commitment, and cautious skepticism from explicit contexts.">
    <h3>Choose ten meaning-and-purpose chunks</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Idiom meaning choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="rings a bell">rings a bell</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="read between the lines">read between the lines</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="misses the point">misses the point</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="break the ice">break the ice</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="get the ball rolling">get the ball rolling</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a step in the right direction">a step in the right direction</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="learn the ropes">learn the ropes</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="easier said than done">easier said than done</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="keep our options open">keep our options open</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="take the claim with a grain of salt">take the claim with a grain of salt</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="prove the claim false">prove the claim false</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The name sounds familiar, but I cannot remember where I heard it. It <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="rings a bell" data-hint="Choose the recognition phrase that does not claim complete recall." data-fix="The familiar name rings a bell.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The email says the schedule is “ambitious” and asks for a contingency plan. To infer the unstated concern about delay, <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="read between the lines" data-hint="Choose the phrase for inferring meaning not stated directly." data-fix="Read between the lines to infer the writer's unstated concern.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>I explained that the measurement was uncertain, but Luis argued about the chart color. He <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="misses the point" data-hint="Choose the phrase for failing to understand the central issue." data-fix="Luis misses the point because he discusses color instead of uncertainty.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>At the first meeting, one low-pressure question helped unfamiliar participants relax and begin talking. It helped <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="break the ice" data-hint="Choose the phrase for reducing initial social tension." data-fix="The opening question helped break the ice.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The agenda is approved, so Maya assigns the first task to <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="get the ball rolling" data-hint="Choose the expression for starting an organized activity." data-fix="The first assigned task gets the ball rolling.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The new ramp fixes one access barrier but not the museum's other wayfinding problems. It is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a step in the right direction" data-hint="Choose a positive evaluation that still signals incomplete progress." data-fix="The ramp is a step in the right direction, not a complete solution.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>During her first week, Nora shadows a colleague to <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="learn the ropes" data-hint="Choose the phrase for learning the basic procedures of a role." data-fix="Nora shadows a colleague to learn the ropes.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>“Just integrate all five systems by Friday” sounds simple, but the technical work is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="easier said than done" data-hint="Choose the response contrasting a simple instruction with difficult execution." data-fix="The integration is easier said than done.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">9</span><span>Two suppliers are still being evaluated, so we will <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="keep our options open" data-hint="Choose the phrase for delaying commitment while alternatives remain useful." data-fix="The team will keep its options open until the evaluation is complete.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">10</span><span>The product claim comes only from an advertisement with no method or source, so <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="take the claim with a grain of salt" data-hint="Choose cautious skepticism, not automatic proof that the claim is false." data-fix="Take the unsupported advertising claim with a grain of salt.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build the grammar around the part that cannot move</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <table><thead><tr><th>Expression</th><th>Stable pattern</th><th>Useful variation</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td>be / get on the same page</td><td><span class="ex">on + the</span></td><td>be more or less on the same page; get the teams on the same page</td></tr>
    <tr><td>break the ice</td><td>definite article <span class="ex">the</span></td><td>breaks, broke, has broken the ice</td></tr>
    <tr><td>cut corners on something</td><td>no article before plural <span class="ex">corners</span></td><td>cut too many corners; cut corners on testing</td></tr>
    <tr><td>draw the line at something</td><td><span class="ex">at + noun / -ing</span></td><td>draws, drew, has drawn the line at sharing data</td></tr>
    <tr><td>keep someone in the loop</td><td>object before <span class="ex">in the loop</span></td><td>keep me, us, the client, or them in the loop</td></tr>
    <tr><td>get the ball rolling</td><td><span class="ex">get + the ball + -ing</span></td><td>gets, got, has gotten the ball rolling in U.S. English</td></tr>
    <tr><td>take something with a grain of salt</td><td>evaluated object before <span class="ex">with</span></td><td>take it, the estimate, or that review with a grain of salt</td></tr>
    <tr><td>read between the lines</td><td>plural <span class="ex">lines</span> with <span class="ex">the</span></td><td>reads, read, has read between the lines</td></tr>
    <tr><td>ring a bell</td><td>the clue is normally the subject</td><td>That rings a bell. Does the name ring any bells?</td></tr>
    <tr><td>play it by ear</td><td>fixed object <span class="ex">it</span></td><td>play, played, or will play it by ear</td></tr>
    <tr><td>call it a day</td><td>fixed <span class="ex">it</span> and article <span class="ex">a</span></td><td>call, called, or should call it a day</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <div class="note"><h3>Fixed does not mean frozen</h3><p>The verb usually changes for tense, aspect, agreement, and modality. Participant slots can change, and some expressions allow degree or descriptive modification. The stable article, preposition, number, complement, or word order often matters more than preserving one dictionary citation form.</p></div>
  <div class="note"><h3>Variation is not automatically an error</h3><p>U.S. English commonly uses <span class="ex">take something with a grain of salt</span>, while <span class="ex">a pinch of salt</span> is also established and common in other varieties. U.S. spelling uses <span class="ex">gray area</span>, while other spelling conventions may differ. Teach the target variety without calling another established variety illogical.</p></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You controlled the fixed preposition, article, complement, participant slot, result pattern, evaluated object, plural noun, recognition subject, and two fixed pronouns while allowing normal verb inflection.">
    <h3>Complete eleven fixed-pattern decisions</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Idiom grammar choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="on the same page">on the same page</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="broke the ice">broke the ice</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="cut corners on">cut corners on</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="draw the line at">draw the line at</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="keep the client in the loop">keep the client in the loop</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="got the ball rolling">got the ball rolling</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="take the estimate with a grain of salt">take the estimate with a grain of salt</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="read between the lines">read between the lines</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="rings a bell">rings a bell</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="play it by ear">play it by ear</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="call it a day">call it a day</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="in a same page">in a same page</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The preview is October 12 and the public launch is October 19. Now we are <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="on the same page" data-hint="Use the fixed preposition and article for shared understanding." data-fix="We are on the same page about the two dates.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Yesterday's informal introduction <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="broke the ice" data-hint="Inflect the verb for past time and retain the definite article." data-fix="The introduction broke the ice yesterday.">choose</button> before the negotiation.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The team saved two hours because it <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="cut corners on" data-hint="Use no article before corners and add the area whose standard was sacrificed." data-fix="The team cut corners on the required inspection.">choose</button> the required inspection.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>I can shorten the meeting, but I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="draw the line at" data-hint="Use the boundary expression followed by at and an -ing form." data-fix="I draw the line at excluding the accessibility reviewer.">choose</button> excluding the accessibility reviewer.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Send a short factual update after each test to <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="keep the client in the loop" data-hint="Place the informed participant before in the loop." data-fix="The updates keep the client in the loop.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>Maya assigned the first task at 9:00, which <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="got the ball rolling" data-hint="Use the past form of get, the fixed object, and the -ing result." data-fix="The first task got the ball rolling.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>The forecast comes from one anonymous post, so <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="take the estimate with a grain of salt" data-hint="Place the evaluated object before the skepticism phrase." data-fix="Take the estimate with a grain of salt.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>The message avoids the word delay but requests a backup date. You have to <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="read between the lines" data-hint="Use the fixed plural noun and definite article for unstated meaning." data-fix="Read between the lines to infer concern about a delay.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">9</span><span>The project name sounds familiar. It <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="rings a bell" data-hint="Make the familiar clue the subject and use the singular verb." data-fix="The project name rings a bell.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">10</span><span>We will decide whether to hold the event outside after we see the weather, so we will <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="play it by ear" data-hint="Use the fixed pronoun in the expression for deciding as events unfold." data-fix="We will play it by ear after checking the weather.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">11</span><span>The urgent tasks are complete and the team will continue tomorrow. Let's <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="call it a day" data-hint="Use the temporary-stopping expression with fixed it and a." data-fix="Let's call it a day and continue tomorrow.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Choose the conversational effect, not the most colorful phrase</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="note"><h3>Register includes relationship, channel, stakes, and evidence</h3><p><span class="ex">Let's get the ball rolling</span> can sound natural in a familiar team meeting. A public safety instruction, legal condition, technical method, or formal incident record usually needs the literal action, agent, standard, and consequence. Formal does not always mean better; explicit means easier to interpret.</p></div>
  <div class="note"><h3>Some familiar idioms can dismiss another person's difficulty</h3><p><span class="ex">It's a piece of cake</span> and <span class="ex">It's not rocket science</span> may be playful about your own task among close colleagues. Said to a struggling learner or worker, they can minimize real difficulty or imply that failure is foolish. Describe the task as <span class="ex">straightforward after training</span> when that is the supported claim.</p></div>
  <div class="note"><h3>One exact idiom is stronger than a cluster</h3><p><span class="cross">Let's break the ice, get the ball rolling, think outside the box, and hit the ground running</span> sounds rehearsed and adds little information. Choose the one interactional purpose that matters, then continue in clear literal language.</p></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You matched alignment, initiation, partial progress, formal incident language, respectful difficulty, categorical rejection, flexible planning, source skepticism, safety clarity, and idiom restraint to ten explicit situations.">
    <h3>Complete ten pragmatics and register decisions</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Idiom pragmatics choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="make sure we are on the same page">make sure we are on the same page</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="get the ball rolling">get the ball rolling</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a step in the right direction">a step in the right direction</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the required clearance was not met">the required clearance was not met</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="straightforward after guided practice">straightforward after guided practice</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="out of the question">out of the question</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="play it by ear">play it by ear</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="take it with a grain of salt">take it with a grain of salt</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="press the red stop button immediately">press the red stop button immediately</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="use one fitting idiom and continue plainly">use one fitting idiom and continue plainly</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="use four metaphors in every sentence">use four metaphors in every sentence</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>At a familiar team meeting, confirm one shared interpretation of the deadline: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="make sure we are on the same page" data-hint="Choose the conversational alignment phrase supported by the date clarification." data-fix="Let's make sure we are on the same page about the deadline.">choose</button>.</span></div>
